{#
  The signed-in reader's section before their books arrive, in the shape it most often takes: one row of
  covers across the width. The loans card is less common, so it has no skeleton: it arrives in the hidden
  `.home-now__loans`, at the row's height, and the row narrows to make room (home-member.css).
  home-member.js fetches the two halves (home/member.html.jinja) and puts each in place of its placeholder as
  it arrives, or takes the placeholder away when that half has nothing to show.
  Signed out it is not displayed (home-member.css).
#}
<section class="home-now home-now--skeleton">
    <span class="shift home-now__loading">{{ _("Loading your books") }}</span>
    <div class="home-now__head" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="skeleton home-now__sk-title"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="home-now__body">
        <div class="home-now__loans" hidden></div>
        <div class="home-now__shelves" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="home-now__label-row">
                <span class="skeleton home-now__sk-line home-now__sk-line--label"></span>
            </div>
            <ul class="home-now__wall">
                {% for _cover in range(14) %}
                    <li>
                        <span class="skeleton home-now__sk-cover"></span>
                    </li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
            <p class="home-now__links">
                <span class="skeleton home-now__sk-line home-now__sk-line--more"></span>
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
